# Analysing a pattern: chosen with a band on the grid, sent over from the spaceship list, or
# typed or pasted as text.
# Expects the default start-up (single rotation, 256×256).
wait 25; clear

# The key opens the panel, choosing a pattern; the pattern card says so.
key a; wait 20
expect_text SelectHint drag over it · Escape cancels
expect_text AnalysisNote Drag over the pattern on the grid. Escape calls it off.
# Before any pattern the panel says what it is for, and nothing else.
expect_shown AnalysisIntro on; expect_shown AnalysisView off; expect_shown StudyWhat off; expect_shown AnalysisPlace off
shot analysis-1-choosing

# A band around the lightest ship, which sits just below and right of the middle of the grid,
# where a drag from the centre of the view begins. The world is at generation 0. The band is
# drawn while the button is down; the study is made when it comes up, on another thread, so
# what it says is waited for.
place $2o2$2o 130 130
move Grid 0 0; press left; move Grid 60 60; wait 3
shot analysis-2-band
release left; wait 20
# The choosing stays on for the next pattern.
expect_text SelectHint drag over it · Escape cancels
expect_text AnalysisNote Drag over another pattern, or Place picks this one up to be put down on the grid where you click.
# What was found is in tiles, each with its name, what it says, and a line more where there
# is more to say. A pattern of one piece has no pieces to tell of.
until expect_text StudyWhat WHAT Spaceship c/6 orthogonal →
expect_text StudyPeriod PERIOD 12 generations moving (2, 0)
expect_text StudyCells CELLS 4
expect_text StudyChanges CHANGES 5.3 cells a generation
expect_text StudySize SIZE 2×3 up to 3×5
expect_text StudySymmetry SYMMETRY a mirror
expect_shown StudyPieces off; expect_shown PiecesList off
expect_text StudyText $2o2$2o
expect_text SmallCaption 42×32 cells, 10 generations a second
shot analysis-3-spaceship

# A band with nothing in it says so.
drag Grid -200 -200; wait 10
expect_text AnalysisNote No live cells in there.
expect_text StudyWhat WHAT Spaceship c/6 orthogonal →
# Nor does a band drawn beside the grid hold anything: here above it, over a cell of the top
# row.
paint 128 0
move Grid -30 -440; press left; move Grid 30 -380; wait 2; release left; wait 10
expect_text AnalysisNote No live cells in there.
paint 128 0 off

# Escape while the band is being drawn calls it off, and what is left of the drag paints
# nothing: the ship's four cells are all there is. The button brings the choosing back.
move Grid 0 0; press left; move Grid 40 40; wait 2; key Escape; wait 2
move Grid 90 20; wait 2; release left; wait 3
expect_population 4
expect_text SelectHint on the grid, or from the list
click Analyse; wait 3

# A band drawn a generation later catches the ship between its blocks, which the study takes
# into account: it is the same ship.
step 1; wait 2
drag Grid 60 60; wait 20
until expect_text StudyWhat WHAT Spaceship c/6 orthogonal →

# The small world runs on its own clock; Pause holds it, and Restart takes it back to the
# pattern as it set out, where it stands still until Play.
click AnalysisPause; wait 3; click AnalysisRestart; wait 10
expect_text SmallStatus generation 0
expect_text AnalysisPause Play
click AnalysisPause; wait 30
expect_text AnalysisPause Pause

# A still life, as single rotation has them: a block lying across two blocks of either
# partition, so that no cell is ever alone in one. (A block in line with the partition is an
# oscillator: it turns about, a cell at a time, where the other partition cuts it in four.)
clear; place 2o$2o 100 101
drag Grid -120 -120; wait 20
until expect_text StudyWhat WHAT Still life
expect_text StudyPeriod PERIOD 1 generation
expect_text StudyCells CELLS 4
expect_text StudyChanges CHANGES none
expect_text StudySymmetry SYMMETRY mirrors both ways and so a half turn
shot analysis-4-still-life

# Copy puts the pattern on the clipboard as text; Place picks it up to be put down on the
# grid, with the stamp, which ends the choosing: here a second block, on the blocks of the
# current partition.
click AnalysisCopy; wait 3; expect_clipboard $2o$2o
expect_text AnalysisNote Copied $2o$2o
click AnalysisPlace; wait 3
expect_text AnalysisNote Click the grid to put the pattern down, as often as you like. Escape or a right click lets go of it.
expect_text SelectHint on the grid, or from the list
click Grid 0 0; wait 3; expect_population 8
key Escape; wait 3
expect_text AnalysisNote Place picks the pattern up, to be put down on the grid where you click.

# A spaceship from the list, by the small button of its row: it is studied as it was filed.
# (Turning catching on opens the list.)
clear; place $2o2$2o 240 120
click Catching; wait 3; step 120; wait 10; expect_caught 1 1
click AnalyseKind0; wait 20
until expect_text StudyWhat WHAT Spaceship c/6 orthogonal →
# The click went to the button alone: the row did not pick the pattern up.
expect_text CatcherNote Click a pattern to pick it up, or shift-click it to copy it as text.
expect_text StudyText b2o2$b2o
shot analysis-5-from-the-list

# The study stays when the rule changes, under the rule named next to the title; Place puts
# the same cells down under the rule now set.
expect_text SubjectRule Single rotation
rule critters; wait 3; expect_text SubjectRule Single rotation
shot analysis-6-another-rule
click AnalysisPlace; wait 3; click Grid 0 0; wait 3; expect_population 4
key Escape; wait 3; expect_rule critters

# Four patterns at once fly apart: what they came to is told piece by piece, and the small
# world's border is open, so that what leaves it is counted.
rule single-rotation; clear
place 2o$2o 90 101; place 3o$o$bo 100 100; place o$o2$o$o 110 100; place $2o2$2o 120 100
click Analyse; wait 3; drag Grid -100 -100; wait 20
# A tile with nothing to say is not there: what does not come back has no period.
until expect_text StudyWhat WHAT Flies apart 513 cells across after 2 882 generations
expect_shown StudyPeriod off; expect_shown StudyChanges off
expect_text StudySize SIZE 32×5 up to 513×196
# The pieces come last, under the buttons. Under their line there is a line to each sort of
# them: how many, what, and the kinds among them.
expect_text StudyPieces 4 pieces
expect_text PieceSort0 3 SPACESHIPS c/15, c/6, c/184
expect_text PieceSort1 1 STILL LIFE
click AnalysisPause; wait 3; click AnalysisRestart; wait 10
expect_text SmallStatus generation 0, no spaceship has left it, 17 cells in it now
click AnalysisPause; wait 3
expect_text StudyText 10b3o7bo$2o8bo9bo9b2o$2o9bo$20bo9b2o$20bo
shot analysis-7-pieces
# A click on the line lists them kind by kind instead, the spaceships, the oscillators and the
# still lifes each under a heading of their own: a kind as the spaceship list shows one
# (period, cells, how many; then its speed, or its size if it stays where it is), with a
# dial of the ways its ships fly. Another click folds the list away again.
click PiecesToggle; wait 3
expect_text StudyPieces 4 pieces
expect_text Piece0 15 5 1 c/15 diagonal
expect_text Piece1 12 4 1 c/6 orthogonal
expect_text Piece2 368 4 1 c/184 diagonal
expect_text Piece3 4 1 2×2
shot analysis-7-pieces-listed
click PiecesToggle; wait 3
expect_text PieceSort1 1 STILL LIFE
click AnalysisCopy; wait 3; expect_clipboard 10b3o7bo$2o8bo9bo9b2o$2o9bo$20bo9b2o$20bo

# A lone cell under the Four-way gun grows into a gun: along lines, and into spaceships.
# (The choosing is still on from the last band.)
rule four-way-gun; wait 2; clear; paint 128 128
drag Grid 20 20; wait 20
until expect_text StudyWhat WHAT Grows along lines, as a gun does 575 cells after 766 generations
# The ships of the four streams are one kind, flying four ways.
expect_text StudyPieces 190 pieces
expect_text PieceSort0 189 SPACESHIPS c/3
expect_text PieceSort1 1 THAT GROWS
click PiecesToggle; wait 3
expect_text Piece0 6 3 189 c/3 diagonal
shot analysis-8-gun
click PiecesToggle; wait 3

# A field of oscillators is back when all of them are at once: after the least common multiple
# of their periods, which is known by the pieces, each followed through its own period. Here a
# cell alone (4 generations), two side by side (16) and three in a corner (36).
rule single-rotation; wait 2; clear; place o9b2o9b2o$20bo 100 110
drag Grid -130 -90; wait 20
until expect_text StudyWhat WHAT Oscillator of 3 pieces that never meet
expect_text StudyPeriod PERIOD 144 generations until all its pieces are back at once
expect_text StudyPieces 3 that never meet
expect_text PieceSort0 3 OSCILLATORS periods 4, 16, 36
expect_text StudyText o9b2o9b2o$20bo
shot analysis-8-many

# The text of a pattern can come from elsewhere: pasted into its field, it is studied under
# the rule of the grid. Here it is the four patterns copied above, under another rule.
rule critters; wait 2
click StudyText; wait 3; key Ctrl+a; key Ctrl+v; wait 10
until expect_text StudyText 10b3o7bo$2o8bo9bo9b2o$2o9bo$20bo9b2o$20bo
expect_text SubjectRule Critters
# A long text goes in at once the same way, from wherever it was copied. This one is what a
# blob of Single rotation left behind inside an open border after two million generations:
# a field of 271 small oscillators and still lifes, which is back after tens of billions.
rule single-rotation; wait 2
clipboard 41bo2$31bo4$36bo6$59bo$44bo5$48bo8bo5$67bo2$59bo6bo2$87bo$62bobo$54bo22bo$72bo29bo2$85bo22bo$61bo$14bo$35bo47b3o$63b2o4bo11bo25bo$36bo$19bo2$46bo$23bo28bo$69bo$27bo5bo3bo12bo$97bo$14bo40bo32bo8bo$52bo20bo$18bo23bo44bo$5bo$102bo$21bo64bo14bo5bo$50bo$51b2o5bo23bo15bo$5bo17bo5bo20b3o33bo5bo$6bo21bobo18bobo$49b2o11b2o$22bo39b2o50bo$11bo3bo3bo28bo31b2o18bo4bo$37bo50bo7bo8bo$24bo15b2o74bo$5bo18bo15b2o16bo40bo9bo$62bo$12bo48bo15b2o$bo25bo31bo17b2o41bo$63bo13bo6bo$49bo6b2o5bo2b2o8bo7bo5b2o$2bo8bo44b3o7b2o8bo13b2o$57b2o18bobo$6bo2bo22bo44b2o21bo$o11bo50bo15b3o35bo$11bo7bobo27b2o10bo18b2o21bo21bo$6bo28bo8bo4b2o49bo$24bo73bo$o17bo12bo81bo$43b2o15bo15bo27bo$40bo2b2o74bo$2bo8bo$36bo77bo$33bo67bo$34bobo4bo45bo$2bo55bo$7bo10bo28bo$28bo22b2o33bo20bo9bo$20bo30b2o3bo2bo44bo11bo$7bo12bo12bo9bo27bo18bo$o21bo3bo4bo48b2o25b2o7bo$21bo58b2o$78b2o16bo3bo$32bo28bo12bo3b2obo41bo$32b2o42bo18bo$32b2o31b4o20bo31bo$65bo2bo28bo14bo$65b3o17bo17bo$90bo$11bo65bo$60b2o31bo$16bo30b2o11bobo13bo$9bo4bo11bo2bo31b2o10bo38bo$18bo52bo$65bo15bo$6bo64b2o$41bo29b2o7bo22bo$99bo$11bo21bo50bo29bo2$53bo45bo28bo$18bo37bo18bo29bo$50bo40bo8bo8bo$54bo22bo13bo$48bo53bo$28bo3bo$38bo26bo4bo36bo$94bo$32bo$25bo22bo34b2o12bo$83b2o25bo$79bo4bo13bo18bo2b2o2$21bo16bo2bo3bo17bo2bo18bo3bo$57bo$19bo37bo26bo18bo9bo$47bo24bo$17bo43bo15bo26bo$22bo13bo37bo32bo2bo$28bo20bo8bo$42bo37b2o18bo11bo$109bo$97bo$21bo73bo$28bo17bo26bo$37bo25bo39bo$56bo$78bo4bo$28bobo14b2o$61bo$60bo34bo$53bo2$107bo$32bo65bo$92bo4bo$99bo2$66bo4bo2$29bo5bo$38bo9bo$45bo25bo$51bo$27bo$40bo$72bo2$23bo3bo
key Ctrl+a; key Ctrl+v; wait 10
until expect_text StudyWhat WHAT Oscillator of 271 pieces that never meet
expect_text StudyPeriod PERIOD 69 481 732 320 generations until all its pieces are back at once
expect_text StudyCells CELLS 415
expect_text StudyChanges CHANGES 592.2 cells a generation 92 never change
expect_text StudyPieces 271 that never meet
expect_text PieceSort0 261 OSCILLATORS periods 4 ×215, 16 ×22, 8 ×8 and 11 more
expect_text PieceSort1 10 STILL LIFES
shot analysis-8-pasted
# Typed, a text is studied as soon as it spells a pattern. What does not spell one is said,
# and Escape leaves the field with the text of the pattern on display, and the choosing on.
key Ctrl+a; type 3o$o$bo; wait 10
until expect_text StudyWhat WHAT Spaceship c/15 diagonal ↘
type x; wait 5
expect_text AnalysisNote 'x' does not belong in a run-length encoded pattern.
shot analysis-8-typed
key Escape; wait 5
expect_text StudyText 3o$o$bo
expect_text AnalysisNote Drag over another pattern, or Place picks this one up to be put down on the grid where you click.

# Close puts the panel away; the key brings it back choosing, and puts it away again. The
# button starts the choosing without closing anything; Escape ends it.
click AnalysisClose; wait 5
key a; wait 5
expect_text AnalysisNote Drag over another pattern, or Place picks this one up to be put down on the grid where you click.
key a; wait 5; shot analysis-9-closed
key a; wait 5
key Escape; wait 3
expect_text AnalysisNote Place picks the pattern up, to be put down on the grid where you click.
expect_text SelectHint on the grid, or from the list
click Analyse; wait 3
expect_text SelectHint drag over it · Escape cancels

# A wide pattern is followed as far as a small one: two lone cells seven hundred cells apart
# are two oscillators, however far that is. (Two side panels leave the grid a third of a
# pixel to the cell.)
rule single-rotation; click GridSize; wait 4; click GridSize:1024; wait 6
clear; paint 150 512; paint 850 512
move Grid -130 -20; press left; move Grid 130 20; wait 2; release left
until expect_text StudyWhat WHAT Oscillator of 2 pieces that never meet
expect_text StudyPieces 2 that never meet
expect_text PieceSort0 2 OSCILLATORS period 4
expect_text StudySize SIZE 701×1

# A study that takes long shows how far it has got, and does not hold up the frames: a
# thousand cells each way of soup would be followed for hours. Stop takes what is known by
# then, and the pattern is on display as any other.
soup
move Grid -150 -150; press left; move Grid 150 150; wait 2; release left
until expect_shown AnalysisStop on
expect_shown AnalysisPause off; expect_shown AnalysisView off; expect_shown StudyWhat off
expect_text AnalysisNote Stop takes what is known by then for the study. A drag over another pattern studies that one instead.
wait 20; shot analysis-10-on-its-way
click AnalysisStop
until expect_shown AnalysisStop off
expect_shown AnalysisPause on; expect_shown AnalysisIntro off
expect_shown StudyPeriod off
shot analysis-11-stopped
click Analyse; wait 3
expect_text SelectHint on the grid, or from the list

# A handful of cells is followed for as long as it takes, within reason. These six are an
# oscillator of 1 068 762 generations, under a rule whose patterns take their time; and four
# others a spaceship that is back, eight cells further up, after 7 328 092.
rule 15,7,6,10,13,12,2,8,14,11,5,4,3,9,1,0; wait 3
click StudyText; wait 3; key Ctrl+a; type $bo2$bo$2bo$bo2b2o; wait 3
until expect_text StudyPeriod PERIOD 1 068 762 generations
expect_text StudyWhat WHAT Oscillator
key Ctrl+a; type bobo$obo; wait 30
expect_shown AnalysisStop on
until expect_text StudyPeriod PERIOD 7 328 092 generations moving (0, -8)
expect_text StudyWhat WHAT Spaceship 2c/1832023 orthogonal ↑
shot analysis-12-slow
key Escape; wait 3
quit
